{"created": "2026-08-30T03:53:22.864682+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-06T11:40:54.081674+00:00", "id": 22168498, "conceptrecid": "22167890", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22168498", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22167890", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22168498", "metadata": {"title": "A Relative Jacobian-Rank Filtration for Keller Maps", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22168498", "publication_date": "2026-08-30", "description": "<p>We introduce the relative Jacobian rank rho_rel(F), the minimum over complex basepoints of the generic rank of JF(x)-JF(a). For complex Keller maps we prove that rho_rel(F) &lt;= 1 implies polynomial automorphy. Consequently every hypothetical nonautomorphic planar Keller map has rho_rel=2. We show that rank two is the first relative-rank stratum permitting nontrivial determinant-balance cancellation and certify rho_rel=3 for an explicit three-dimensional noninjective Keller map from the 2026 counterexample literature. The paper does not claim rho_rel(F) &lt;= 2 implies automorphism. Exact symbolic verification is supplementary.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Atwell, Casey", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Jacobian conjecture", "Keller map", "polynomial automorphism", "Jacobian rank", "nilpotent Jacobian", "affine invariant"], "dates": [{"type": "created"}], "references": ["H. Bass, E. H. Connell, D. Wright,    \"The Jacobian conjecture: reduction of degree and formal expansion of the inverse\"    Identifier: DOI 10.1090/S0273-0979-1982-15032-7", "H. Guo, M. de Bondt, X. Du, X. Sun,    \"Polynomial maps with invertible sums of Jacobian matrices and directional derivatives\"    Identifier: DOI 10.1016/j.indag.2011.11.007", "X. Sun,    \"On additive-nilpotency of Jacobian matrices of polynomial maps\"    Identifier: DOI 10.1016/j.laa.2013.10.014", "M. de Bondt, X. Sun,    \"Classification of cubic homogeneous polynomial maps with Jacobian matrices of rank two\"    Identifier: DOI 10.1017/S0004972718000345", "S. Gao, 